as a la inteligencia artificial. Mejora tu productividad con esta herramienta innovadora","fr":"Stage est la façon élégante d''accéder à Anki, grâce à l''intelligence artificielle. Améliorez votre productivité avec cet outil innovant","de":"Stage ist der stilvolle Weg zu Anki, dank Künstlicher Intelligenz. Verbessern Sie Ihre Produktivität mit diesem innovativen Tool","pt":"O Stage é uma ferramenta de IA que oferece uma abordagem inovadora para Anki, melhorando a experiência do usuário","ru":"Stage - это инструмент ИИ, который предлагает инновационный подход к Anki, улучшая опыт пользователя","ar":"Stage هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي تقدم نهجًا مبتكرًا لبرنامج Anki، مما يحسن تجربة المستخدم","en":"The swanky way to Anki"},"definition":{"en":"The swanky way to Anki"},"features":{"zh":["高级学习算法","个性化学习计划","智能卡片生成","多平台支持","简单易用的界面"],"ja":["高度な学習アルゴリズム","個人化された学習プラン","智能カード生成","マルチプラットフォーム対応","シンプルな操作性"],"ko":["고급 학습 알고리즘","개인화된 학습 계획","지능형 카드 생성","멀티 플랫폼 지원","간단한 사용자 인터페이스"],"es":["Integración con Anki","Interfaz de usuario intuitiva","Funcionalidades de inteligencia artificial","Mejora de la productividad","Compatibilidad con dispositivos móviles"],"fr":["Intégration avec Anki","Interface utilisateur intuitive","Fonctionnalités d''intelligence artificielle","Amélioration de la productivité","Compatibilité avec les appareils mobiles"],"de":["Integration mit Anki","Benutzerfreundliche Oberfläche","Funktionen der künstlichen Intelligenz","Verbesserung der Produktivität","Kompatibilität mit mobilen Geräten"],"pt":["Integração com Anki","Recursos de aprendizado personalizados","Interface de usuário intuitiva","Suporte a múltiplos dispositivos","Análise de desempenho detalhada"],"ru":["Интеграция с Anki","Персонализированные функции обучения","Интуитивно понятный интерфейс","Поддержка нескольких устройств","Детальный анализ производительности"],"ar":["التكامل مع برنامج Anki","ميزات تعلم مخصصة","واجهة مستخدم سهلة الاستخدام","دعم الأجهزة المتعددة","تحليل أداء مفصل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用stage","stage和Anki的区别","stage安装指南","stage设置教程","AI智能工具","学习效率提高","stage替代工具","stage vs Anki"],"ja":["stageの使い方","stageとAnkiの違い","stageのインストール方法","stageの設定ガイド","AIエージェント","学習効率の向上","stageの代替ツール","stage vs Anki"],"ko":["stage 사용법","stage와 Anki의 차이","stage 설치 가이드","stage 설정 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트","학습 효율 향상","stage 대체 툴","stage vs Anki"],"es":["cómo usar Stage","qué es Stage","Stage vs Anki","alternativas a Anki","instalación de Stage","guía de configuración de Stage","herramientas de IA para productividad"],"fr":["comment utiliser Stage","qu''est-ce que Stage","Stage vs Anki","alternatives à Anki","installation de Stage","guide de configuration de Stage","outils IA pour la productivité"],"de":["wie man Stage verwendet","was ist Stage","Stage vs Anki","Alternativen zu Anki","Installation von Stage","Konfigurationsanleitung für Stage","KI-Tools für Produktivität"],"pt":["o que é stage","ferramentas de ia para anki","como usar stage","stage vs anki","instalar stage","guia de configuração do stage","recursos de aprendizado personalizados","integração com anki"],"ru":["что такое stage","инструменты ии для anki","как использовать stage","stage vs anki","установить stage","руководство по настройке stage","персонализированные функции обучения","интеграция с anki"],"ar":["ما هو.Stage","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لبرنامج Anki","كيفية استخدام.Stage","Stage مقابل Anki","تثبيت.Stage","دليل إعداد.Stage","ميزات التعلم المخصصة","التكامل مع برنامج Anki"]}},"owner":"Mjvolk3","repo":"Swanki","repoPath":"Mjvolk3/Swanki","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T20:38:24Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"stage","description":"Smart staging with auto-detected file blocks and interactive override. Use before /commit.","bodyPreview":"# Smart Stage\n\nStage files for commit using auto-detected logical blocks. The user picks which blocks to stage via interactive selection.\n\n## Workflow\n\n```\n/stage -> /commit\n```\n\n## Step 1: Scan unstaged/untracked files\n\nRun `git status` (never use `-uall` flag) to get the full picture of modified, deleted, and untracked files.\n\nIf there are no unstaged or untracked changes, inform the user and stop.\n\n## Step 2: Auto-detect file blocks\n\nGroup related files into logical blocks based on these rule","body":"# Smart Stage\n\nStage files for commit using auto-detected logical blocks. The user picks which blocks to stage via interactive selection.\n\n## Workflow\n\n```\n/stage -> /commit\n```\n\n## Step 1: Scan unstaged/untracked files\n\nRun `git status` (never use `-uall` flag) to get the full picture of modified, deleted, and untracked files.\n\nIf there are no unstaged or untracked changes, inform the user and stop.\n\n## Step 2: Auto-detect file blocks\n\nGroup related files into logical blocks based on these rules (applied in order of priority):\n\n### The Commit Trio rule\n\nAny block that contains a `.py` file under `swanki/` or `tests/` MUST also include:\n\n1. The paired dendron note (`notes/<dendron-path>.md`) -- if it exists in the changed file list\n2. The paired test file (`tests/.../<test_file>.py`) or source file -- if it exists in the changed file list\n3. The current weekly note (`notes/user.mjvolk3.swanki.tasks.weekly.*.md`) -- always pulled into any block containing Python files\n\nThe weekly note appears in the FIRST Python block only (not duplicated across blocks). This enforces the project''s atomic commit rule: source + note + weekly travel together.\n\n### Block detection rules (in priority order)\n\n1. **Python trio**: a `.py` source file + its `notes/<dendron-path>.md` + its `tests/` counterpart + the weekly note. Multiple related `.py` files in the same package can be grouped into one block (e.g., all files under `swanki/processing/`).\n2. **Skill bundles**: all files under a `.claude/skills/<name>/` directory grouped together\n3. **Config clusters**: related config files (e.g., `.pre-commit-config.yaml` + `pyproject.toml` when both have lint-related changes)\n4. **Shell scripts + notes**: `.sh` files paired with their `notes/scripts.<name>.md` counterpart\n5. **Standalone notes**: `notes/*.md` files not already paired with Python or shell files\n6. **Other files**: anything not covered above (configs, docs, etc.)\n\nA file should only appear in one block. If a file could fit multiple blocks, use the highest-priority rule.\n\n## Step 3: Present blocks to user\n\nDisplay numbered blocks with file lists. Mark the weekly note explicitly so the user sees it:\n\n```\nDetected file blocks:\n[1] Processing package (4 files):\n    swanki/processing/pdf_processor.py\n    swanki/processing/image_processor.py\n    notes/swanki.processing.pdf_processor.md\n    notes/user.mjvolk3.swanki.tasks.weekly.2026.08.md  (weekly)\n[2] Scripts: scripts/dendron-tree.sh\n[3] Standalone notes: notes/scratch.2026.02.11.*.md (3 files)\n```\n\n## Step 4: User picks blocks\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with `multiSelect: true` to let the user choose which blocks to stage. Options:\n\n- Each detected block as a selectable option\n- \"All\" to stage everything\n\n## Step 5: Pre-stage reminders\n\nPrint reminders as informational text (not blocking):\n\n- If selected files include `.py` under `swanki/` or `tests/`: \"Python files detected. Consider running `/update-py-notes` and `/ruff` first.\"\n\n## Step 6: Stage selected blocks\n\n- Run `git add <files>` for chosen blocks (explicit file paths, never `git add -A` or `git add .`)\n- Use `git rm` for deleted files\n- Never stage `.env`, credentials, or secrets -- warn the user if detected\n\n## Step 7: Confirm\n\nRun `git diff --cached --name-status` to show what is now staged.\n\n## Important Rules\n\n- NEVER run `git add -A` or `git add .`\n- NEVER stage `.env`, credentials, secrets, or similar sensitive files -- warn the user\n- Use `git rm` for deleted files\n- The user''s tool approval prompt is the gate -- do NOT ask extra confirmation questions\n- A file appears in exactly one block\n- Do NOT ask extra approval questions -- tool approval prompts are the gates\n- The weekly note is always included with the first Python block -- never staged alone as a separate block when Python files are present\n\n## Example Invocations\n\n- `/stage` -- interactive staging of all changes\n- \"stage my changes\"\n- \"stage files for commit\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T04:00:42.823Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Version Control Agents needing efficient Git workflow management.","zh":"非常适合需要高效Git工作流管理的版本控制代理。","ja":"バージョン管理エージェントが効率的なGitワークフロー管理を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"효율적인 Git 워크플로우 관리가 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de control de versiones que necesitan una gestión eficiente del flujo de trabajo de Git.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de contrôle de version nécessitant une gestion efficace du workflow Git.","de":"Perfekt für Version Control Agents, die eine effiziente Git-Workflow-Verwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Controle de Versão que precisam de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho Git eficiente.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов контроля версий, которым требуется эффективное управление рабочим процессом Git.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة تدفق عمل Git فعال"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate Git staging using auto-detected logical blocks, streamlining the commit process with interactive selection and `git status` analysis.","zh":"赋予代理自动化Git暂存使用自动检测的逻辑块，通过交互选择和`git status`分析简化提交过程。","ja":"エージェントに自動検出された論理ブロックを使用したGitステージングの自動化を可能にし、インタラクティブ選択と`git status`分析によってコミットプロセスを簡素化します。","ko":"자동 감지된 논리 블록을 사용하여 Git 스테이징 자동화를 가능하게 하며, 상호 작용 선택과 `git status` 분석을 통해 커밋 프로세스를 단순화합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes automatizar la configuración de Git utilizando bloques lógicos auto-detectados, simplificando el proceso de confirmación con selección interactiva y análisis de `git status`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser la mise en scène de Git à l''aide de blocs logiques auto-détectés, simplifiant le processus de validation avec une sélection interactive et une analyse de `git status`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Git-Stage-Automatisierung mithilfe von auto-erkannten logischen Blöcken zu automatisieren, strafft den Commit-Prozess mit interaktiver Auswahl und `git status`-Analyse.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar o estágio Git usando blocos lógicos auto-detectados, simplificando o processo de confirmação com seleção interativa e análise de `git status`.","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать стейджинг Git с помощью автоматически обнаруживаемых логических блоков, оптимизируя процесс фиксации с помощью интерактивного выбора и анализа `git status`.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من توفير آلي لمرحلة Git باستخدام الكتل المنطقية المكتشفة تلقائيًا، وباستخدام التحديد التفاعلي وتحليل `git status`"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating staging of modified files","Grouping related files into logical blocks","Streamlining the commit process with interactive selection"],"zh":["自动化修改文件的暂存","将相关文件分组为逻辑块","通过交互选择简化提交过程"],"ja":["変更されたファイルのステージングを自動化する","関連ファイルを論理ブロックにグループ化する","インタラクティブ選択によってコミットプロセスを簡素化する"],"ko":["수정된 파일의 스테이징 자동화","관련 파일을 논리 블록으로 그룹화","상호 작용 선택으로 커밋 프로세스 단순화"],"es":["Automatizar la configuración de archivos modificados","Agrupar archivos relacionados en bloques lógicos","Simplificar el proceso de confirmación con selección interactiva"],"fr":["Automatiser la mise en scène de fichiers modifiés","Regrouper des fichiers liés en blocs logiques","Simplifier le processus de validation avec une sélection interactive"],"de":["Automatisieren der Staging von geänderten Dateien","Gruppieren von verwandten Dateien in logische Blöcke","Straffen des Commit-Prozesses mit interaktiver Auswahl"],"pt":["Automatizar o estágio de arquivos modificados","Agrupar arquivos relacionados em blocos lógicos","Simplificar o processo de confirmação com seleção interativa"],"ru":["Автоматизация стейджинга измененных файлов","Группировка связанных файлов в логические блоки","Оптимизация процесса фиксации с помощью интерактивного выбора"],"ar":["توفير آلي لمرحلة الملفات المعدلة","تجميع الملفات المرتبطة في كتل منطقية","تبسيط عملية الإلتزام مع التحديد التفاعلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation","Limited to Git version control system"],"zh":["需要Git安装","仅限于Git版本控制系统"],"ja":["Gitのインストールが必要","Gitバージョン管理システムにのみ限られている"],"ko":["Git 설치 필요","Git 버전 제어 시스템에만限됨"],"es":["Requiere instalación de Git","Limitado al sistema de control de versiones Git"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Git","Limité au système de contrôle de version Git"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation","Begrenzt auf das Git-Version-Control-System"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Git","Limitado ao sistema de controle de versão Git"],"ru":["Требуется установка Git","Ограничен только системой контроля версий Git"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Git","محدود بنظام التحكم في الإصدار Git"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"723783aa150a4c129f33f1c916c777b9a768e7041fbb2f2be569273947de8bb5","qualityScore":28}');
